---
import PortfolioLayout from '../layouts/PortfolioLayout.astro';
import ThemeToggle from '../components/portfolio/ThemeToggle.astro';
import EmojiReaction from '../components/portfolio/EmojiReaction.astro';
import ProjectPreview from '../components/portfolio/ProjectPreview.astro';
import ColourSampler from '../components/portfolio/ColourSampler.astro';
import '../styles/portfolio.css';
---
<PortfolioLayout>
<main id="main-content" class="compact-page" tabindex="-1">
<nav class="portfolio-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/cv/">CV</a><ThemeToggle /></nav>
    <header class="compact-header"><h1>Paolo Papania<span class="compact-period">.</span></h1><span class="compact-location">Aarhus, Denmark</span></header>
    <section class="compact-intro" aria-label="Introduction">
      <p>I’m a <span class="compact-inline compact-code"><span aria-hidden="true">&#123; &#125;</span> frontend engineer</span> who cares about how things <span class="compact-feel">feel.</span> My work brings together UX/UI development, <span class="compact-design">product design</span> and the code that makes it all work.</p>
      <p>I like taking something from <span class="compact-idea">“what if?”</span> to <span class="compact-built">“that works.”</span> Figuring out the problem, shaping the interface, and getting <EmojiReaction /> right.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="compact-section" id="about"><h2>Currently</h2><p>I work on the app at <a class="compact-inline compact-studiz" href="#studiz"><span aria-hidden="true">s.</span> Studiz</a>, using Angular, Ionic and Capacitor. My role spans frontend development, interface design and the everyday decisions that turn a feature into a useful product.</p></section>
    <section class="compact-section" id="work"><div class="compact-section-heading"><h2>A little of my work</h2><span>Open an entry to read more</span></div>
      <div class="compact-work-group"><span class="compact-year">Now</span><div class="compact-entries">
        <details id="studiz" class="compact-entry"><summary><span class="compact-entry-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><span>Building the Studiz app</span><span class="compact-tag">Frontend</span><span class="compact-expand" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="compact-entry-body"><p>I’m the app developer at Studiz, working with Angular, Ionic and Capacitor. The app connects students with features including digital student ID, events, lending and discounts.</p><p>My work sits where interface design meets implementation: building features, refining interactions and working with the backend team to bring them together.</p><span class="compact-tools">Angular / Ionic / Capacitor / UX/UI</span></div></details>
      </div></div>
      <div class="compact-work-group"><span class="compact-year">Earlier</span><div class="compact-entries">
        <details class="compact-entry"><summary><span class="compact-entry-icon rust" aria-hidden="true">↳</span><span>RaskRask Recharge</span><span class="compact-tag">Product</span><span class="compact-expand" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="compact-entry-body"><p>A thesis project exploring how a wellness service could improve its booking experience and business operations. My work connected UX research, user flows and interface design.</p><button class="compact-preview" data-project="0">See the project preview <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div></details>
        <details class="compact-entry"><summary><span class="compact-entry-icon olive" aria-hidden="true">⊞</span><span>Harmony UI</span><span class="compact-tag">Design system</span><span class="compact-expand" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="compact-entry-body"><p>A shared visual language for RaskRask’s digital products, developed during my internship. Visual foundations and reusable interface components help the product feel consistent.</p><button class="compact-preview" data-project="1">See the project preview <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div></details>
      </div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="compact-section"><h2>Things I care about</h2><p>Interfaces that <span class="compact-underline">make sense.</span> Code someone else can read. A button that responds just right. Understanding why we’re building something before deciding how.</p><p>I’m interested in the space between <span class="compact-thin">the big picture</span> and <strong class="compact-weight">the small details.</strong></p></section>
    <section class="compact-section"><h2>Off screen</h2><p>Usually somewhere between a <span class="compact-inline compact-keyboard"><span aria-hidden="true">⌨</span> split keyboard</span>, a rugby pitch <span class="compact-rugby" aria-hidden="true">🏉</span>, and family life. South African, with Italian roots, now based in Denmark.</p></section>
    <section class="compact-section compact-connect"><h2>Connect</h2><p>For a little more background, <a href="/cv/">read my CV <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>.</p><p>Have something in mind? Say hello by <a href="mailto:papaniap11@gmail.com">email</a>, or find my code on <a href="https://github.com/PapaniaP" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>.</p></section>
    <footer class="compact-footer" style="flex-wrap:wrap"><span>Paolo Papania © {new Date().getFullYear()}</span><span>Thought through. Built with care.</span><ColourSampler /></footer>
  </main>
<ProjectPreview />
<script>
  const studiz = document.querySelector<HTMLDetailsElement>('#studiz');
  document.querySelector('a[href="#studiz"]')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (studiz) studiz.open = true;
  });
</script>
</PortfolioLayout>
